      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f5bb2ae5-440a-5bc6-8a2b-9e9bd4aa9ac4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Military Units: Companion cavalry, 4th Infantry Division (Russian Empire)\n- People: Philip II of Macedon, Alexander the Great\n- Concepts: shock cavalry, shock troops, assault troops\n\nFacts:\n- The Companion cavalry, or hetairoi, were the elite cavalry of the Macedonian army from the time of Philip II of Macedon.\n- Under Alexander the Great, the Companion cavalry achieved their greatest prestige.\n- The Companion cavalry have been regarded as the best cavalry in the ancient world and as the first shock cavalry.\n- Shock troops, also called assault troops, are formations created to lead an attack.\n- In June 1917, the 4th Infantry Division of the Russian Empire was designated the 4th Infantry Shock Division after being reformed as a shock troop unit.\n- In July 1917, the unit became known as the 4th Infantry Shock Division of Death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8c40a5e1-b8de-558d-9cee-38157bee47ce",
        "text": "Page: Companion cavalry. Sentence: The Companions (Greek: , hetairoi) were the elite cavalry of the Macedonian army from the time of king Philip II of Macedon, achieved their greatest prestige under Alexander the Great, and have been regarded as the best cavalry in the ancient world and the first shock cavalry.\nPage: Shock troops. Sentence: Shock troops or assault troops are formations created to lead an attack.\nPage: 4th Infantry Division (Russian Empire). Sentence: In June 1917, it was designated as the 4th Infantry Shock Division (4-я пехотная ударная дивизия) upon being reformed as a shock troop unit and the following month it became known as the 4th Infantry Shock Division of Death (4-я пехотная ударная дивизия смерти).",
